meta {
  name: Get Deployment
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
}

docs {
  Returns one deployment with optional live orchestrator status. RBAC scoping mirrors List Deployments:
    PlatformAdmin : any deployment
    OrgAdmin      : deployments in their organisation
    everyone else : only their own (deployer_user_id = caller)

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required — 401 if no principal.
    2. Parse deployment ID — 404 if invalid UUID or not found.
    3. Apply RBAC visibility check — 403 if caller lacks access.
    4. Enrich response with app_slug (from App row) and values_schema (from AppVersion row)
       so the frontend can render the reconfigure form without extra requests.
    5. When the deployment has a last_argocd_app_name and is not in a terminal state,
       poll Orchestrator.Status synchronously and include live_status:
       { phase, message, last_synced_at, revision, healthy }.
       Orchestrator failures are silenced — the persisted DB state is authoritative.

  Responses:
    200 OK        — deployment row with app_slug, values_schema, and optional live_status
    401 unauthorized — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden — caller cannot see this deployment
    404 not_found — deployment not found
}
